  m_Name: L13_CinSeddi
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Cutrium.Presentation::Cutrium.Presentation.Landmark.LandmarkDefinition
  _landmarkId: cin-seddi
  _displayTitle: Great Wall of China
  _shortDescription: The Great Wall is not one continuous wall, but a vast defensive
    network built by different dynasties over many centuries. Its walls, passes,
    and watchtowers form a system spanning thousands of kilometres. Depending on
    the region, builders used rammed earth, stone, or brick, while smoke, fire, and
    flag signals carried messages rapidly between towers.
  _sector: CHINA
  _displayTitleTurkish: "\xC7in Seddi"
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "\xC7in Seddi tek ve kesintisiz bir duvar de\u011Fil,
    farkl\u0131 hanedanlar\u0131n y\xFCzy\u0131llar boyunca kurdu\u011Fu geni\u015F
    bir savunma a\u011F\u0131d\u0131r. Duvarlar, ge\xE7itler ve g\xF6zetleme kuleleri
    binlerce kilometrelik bir sistem olu\u015Fturur. B\xF6lgeye g\xF6re s\u0131k\u0131\u015Ft\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015F
    toprak, ta\u015F ya da tu\u011Fla kullan\u0131lan kulelerde duman, ate\u015F
    ve bayrak sinyalleriyle haberler h\u0131zla aktar\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131."
  _sectorTurkish: "\xC7\u0130N"
  _artwork: {fileID: 8068504576610999302, guid: 2639107870faa1c489a99e330fa563d2, type: 3}
